  "part_of_speech": "adverb / na-adjective / suru-verb",
  "gloss": "vaguely, absent-mindedly",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "suru",
    "prefix": "ぼんやり"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "vaguely, dimly",
      "explanation": "Not clearly; indistinctly."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "absent-mindedly, in a daze",
      "explanation": "Without focus or attention; spacing out."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex1",
      "japanese": "ぼんやり{見|み}える。",
      "english": "It looks dim.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex2",
      "japanese": "{遠|とお}くの{山|やま}がぼんやり{見|み}える。",
      "english": "The distant mountains can be seen dimly.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex3",
      "japanese": "{霧|きり}で{景色|けしき}がぼんやりしている。",
      "english": "The scenery looks hazy because of the fog.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex4",
      "japanese": "ぼんやりと{窓|まど}の{外|そと}を{見|み}ていた。",
      "english": "I was gazing absent-mindedly out the window.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex5",
      "japanese": "ぼんやりしていて{電車|でんしゃ}を{乗|の}り{過|す}ごした。",
      "english": "I was spacing out and missed my train stop.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03727_bonyari_ex6",
      "japanese": "{休|やす}みの{日|ひ}は{何|なに}もしないでぼんやり{過|す}ごした。",
      "english": "I spent my day off doing nothing, just idling away.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "An onomatopoeic word with multiple related uses.\n\nPATTERNS:\n・ぼんやり(と)する (to space out, to be vague)\n・ぼんやり(と){見|み}える (to be dimly visible)\n・ぼんやりした + noun (vague, hazy)\n\nCOMMON USES:\n・ぼんやりした{記憶|きおく} (vague memory)\n・ぼんやりした{輪郭|りんかく} (blurry outline)\n・ぼんやり{過|す}ごす (to spend time idly)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・うっかり - carelessly (implies a mistake)\n・ぼんやり - absent-mindedly (implies lack of focus)\n・ぼーっと - spaced out, zoning out",
